ure unmanned submersible, and thermohygrometer. The seawater transparency tester is used to monitor suspended particles, organic matter, and chemicals in the sea; the electronic counter can be used to count the number of marine organisms; the benthic miniature unmanned submersible is used to obtain information about ocean bottom sediments and marine communities; the thermohygrometer is used to measure the temperature, salinity, and humidity of seawater."}', 'reference': 'Common underwater imaging equipment includes sonar imaging systems, video camera systems, laser three-dimensional scanners, and so on.'}{'question': 'Edit a big data report used for analyzing marine ecosystems.', 'answer': '\n\n**Title:** "Big Data-Driven Analysis of Marine Ecosystem Dynamics and Conservation Strategies"  \n\n**Abstract:**  \nThis report leverages big data analytics to examine critical factors influencing marine ecosystems, including biodiversity trends, water quality metrics, and climate change impacts. By integrating multidisciplinary datasets, the study identifies emerging threats, such as habitat degradation and species vulnerability, while proposing data-informed strategies for sustainable marine resource management. The findings underscore the urgency of adopting adaptive policies and technological innovations to mitigate ecological risks and ensure long-term ocean health.  \n\n---  \n*Note: The edited title and abstract emphasize the role of big data, align with the context’s focus on scientific management, and highlight actionable insights for marine conservation.*', 'contexts': 't will have certain impacts on the marine ecological environment, thus necessitating the adoption of scientific management and protection measures."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Title: An Investigation Report on Marine Research\\n\\nAbstract: This report provides an in-depth analysis of our recent investigation into marine ecosystems. Covering diverse key aspects such as biodiversity, water quality, and the impact of climate change, the report serves to highlight our scientific findings, potential challenges, and subsequent recommendations to promote the sustainable management and conservation of marine resources.", "output": "Title: \\"Oceanographic Report: Unveiling the Mysteries of the South China Sea Deep-Sea Ecosystem.\\" \\n\\nAbstract: This report focuses on the South China Sea deep-sea as the subject of research, revealing the rare living creatures in the deep-sea environment and their adaptations. The research findings will have significant implications for biodiversity conservation and marine environmental governance."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why does a typhoon cause strong winds and huge waves?", "output": "Typhoons inherently come with extreme wind force and storm surges, and they are affected by various factors such as terrain, ocean temperature, and atmospheric pressure. This often leads to strong winds and large waves, posing significant hazards and impacts on marine navigation and coastal areas."}\n', 'reference': 'Important parameters that can be tracked in marine ecosystems include water temperature, salinity, direction of waves, quantity and species of plankton, rate of ocean acidification, etc. In marine big data analysis, we use these data to train machine learning algorithms to understand the changes in the marine ecosystem, forecast potential environmental changes, etc. By utilizing these critical parameters, we can perceive the panorama and pattern of the marine ecosystem and extract valuable information from it to support adaptive and sustainable management practices in the ocean.'}{'question': 'Describe the main methods of underwater mineral exploration.', 'answer': "\n\nThe main methods of underwater mineral exploration include **geophysical prospecting**, **sonar detection**, and **mineralogical analysis**.  \n\n1. **Geophysical Prospecting**: This involves techniques such as geomagnetism, gravity surveys, and electromagnetic methods to detect subsurface mineral deposits by analyzing variations in Earth's physical properties.  \n2. **Sonar Detection**: Utilizes sound waves to map seafloor topography, identify underwater geological structures, and detect seafloor materials or rock formations through echo analysis.  \n3. **Mineralogical Analysis**: Employs modern analytical tools to study the chemical composition of rocks and minerals, as well as the morphology and structure of mineral crystals, to determine their economic viability.  \n\nThese methods are combined to assess the distribution, type, and potential value of underwater mineral resources.", 'contexts': 'ean big data technology can also be used to formulate marine environment protection and management plans, promoting sustainable marine development."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What are the technologies for underwater mineral exploration?", "output": "Underwater mineral exploration technologies include a variety of methods such as geophysical prospecting, sonar detection, and mineralogical analysis. Among these, geophysical prospecting involves methods such as geomagnetism, gravity, and electromagnetism. Sonar detection is used to determine seafloor topography, seafloor matter, underwater rocks, and geological structures from echoes. Mineralogical analysis involves using modern analytical techniques to analyze the chemical composition of rocks and minerals as well as the morphology of mineral crystals."}{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Provide the latest information on the submarine cable construction in the east sea area.", "output": "According to the latest data, an underwater optical cable connecting China and Japan is currently under construction in the East China Sea, expected to be completed by 2022."}\n', 'reference': 'The main methods for undersea mineral detection currently include: sonic detection, magnetic detection, electromagnetic wave detection, and gravity detection. Among them, sonic detection is generally used for the survey of seabed topography and morphology; magnetic detection can be used to detect undersea magnetic materials, such as geothermal resources identification; electromagnetic wave detection technology can be used to find undersea hydrothermal vents, etc.; while gravity detection technology can help discover undersea mineral resources and sediments, etc.'}{'question': 'I would like to know information about major ports in China. Could you recommend some websites or apps for me?', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain information about websites or apps that provide details on major ports in China. I don't know specific recommendations for this query.", 'contexts': 'on", "input": "May I know which one is the largest fishing port in China?", "output": "The largest fishing port in China is Yujia Port in Shandong."}\n{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "Recommend some outstanding companies that construct undersea cables in the east sea area.", "output": "Outstanding companies such as China Telecom, China Mobile, China Unicom, and China National Offshore Oil Corporation are engaged in the construction of submarine cables in the East China Sea region. These companies have a wealth of experience and technical advantages in the design, construction, and maintenance of submarine cables, which can provide reliable support for the communication services in the East China Sea region. In addition, these companies also pay attention to environmental protection and social responsibilities, actively participating in marine environmental protection and public welfare activities."}{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify which of the following variables is part of the ocean environment\'s dynamic process: ① photosynthesis rate; ② salinity; ③ water temperature; ④ air pressure.", "output": "The answer is ②Salinity. Salinity is a very important variable in the dynamical processes of the marine environment, which can affect the density, circulation, and mixing processes of the water body in the ocean."}\n', 'reference': 'I recommend that you use the "China Ports Window" APP or the China Maritime Bureau website, both of which can provide detailed information about major ports in China.'}{'question': "Why isn't seawater just simply water?", 'answer': '\n\nSeawater is not simply water because it contains a high concentration of dissolved salts and minerals. Over long geological history, seawater has accumulated salts from sources such as continental erosion, atmospheric deposition, and other natural processes. These minerals are continuously added through filtration and interaction with the environment, making seawater a complex solution rather than pure H₂O. In contrast, river water undergoes physical and chemical filtration and sedimentation on land, resulting in lower mineral content and a fresher composition.', 'contexts': 'e sustainable use. At the same time, the modernization of fisheries should be promoted to enhance the efficiency and quality of fishery production."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why is seawater saltier than river water?", "output": "The reason why seawater is saltier than river water is mainly due to the fact that over a long geological history, seawater has been filtered and stirred, constantly absorbing salts from the continents and air. On the other hand, river water originates from the interiors of lands. Due to various physical and chemical filtration and sedimentation processes, it contains lower amounts of trace minerals. Therefore, river water is relatively fresh compared to seawater."}{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Analyze the trend of changes in the topography and terrain of the seabed along the coast of zhejiang.", "output": "The changes in the topography and landforms along the coast of Zhejiang are inseparably linked to rising sea levels and geological activities. In recent years, the changes in the seabed topography and landforms have been intensified by factors such as extreme weather, marine floating objects, and human activities. It is necessary to strengthen monitoring and analysis to ensure the balance between regional development and the marine environment."}\n', 'reference': 'Seawater is a type of saltwater that not only contains water but also contains thousands of elements and compounds, including salts, minerals, trace elements, and biological organic matter. The interactions between these elements are extremely complex and are crucial to the ecological environment and ecosystem development of the ocean.'}{'question': 'What is a tropical storm?', 'answer': '\n\nA tropical storm is a type of cyclone with relatively weak circulation, typically characterized by intense rainfall and storm surges. It forms under specific conditions, such as high sea surface temperatures and low atmospheric pressure.', 'contexts': 'd perception, data fusion, and other methods, it can provide more precise and reliable support for marine forecasting, sea rescue, and other needs."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Briefly explain the formation and characteristics of tropical storms.", "output": "A tropical storm is a type of cyclone with relatively weak circulation, usually characterized by intense rainfall and storm surges. Its formation requires certain conditions, such as high sea temperatures and low air pressure."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "What submarine cables are there in the East Sea region?", "output": "There are multiple undersea cables in the East China Sea region, including Infinera\'s Shanghai-Tokyo Transmission System, China Unicom\'s International East China Sea Optical Cable Phase 2 Project, and Hong Kong Telecom\'s East China Sea PCCW Optical Cable, etc. These cables not only provide broadband access channels for the Internet, but also provide infrastructure security for the application of various new information technologies."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "How do environmental organizations use remote sensing data for ocean monitoring?", "output": "Environmental organizations can analyze remote sensing data for possible pollutants in the ocean and air quality data, in order to take timely measures to protect the marine environment."}\n', 'reference': 'A tropical storm is a cyclonic weather system that occurs in tropical regions, forming over tropical oceans, primarily triggered by alternating cold and warm, humid air masses.'}{'question': 'Analyze what positive impacts can the use of marine big data technology have on aspects such as the marine environment and ecology?', 'answer': '\n\nThe use of marine big data technology can have several positive impacts on the marine environment and ecology, as highlighted in the provided context:  \n\n1. **Enhanced Monitoring and Protection**: By analyzing marine pollutants and ecological states, big data enables real-time monitoring of environmental changes, helping to identify and mitigate threats such as pollution, overfishing, or habitat degradation.  \n\n2. **Climate Change Prediction and Mitigation**: Big data improves the accuracy of predicting marine climate changes (e.g., sea level rise, temperature shifts), allowing proactive measures to reduce harm to ecosystems and human activities.  \n\n3. **Sustainable Resource Management**: It supports informed decision-making for the sustainable exploitation of marine resources (e.g., oil, wind energy, aquaculture) by balancing economic development with ecological preservation.  \n\n4. **Ecological Risk Assessment**: Advanced data analysis helps assess the health of marine ecosystems, guiding conservation efforts and policies to protect biodiversity and restore damaged habitats.  \n\n5. **Human Activity Regulation**: By analyzing human impacts (e.g., shipping, coastal development), big data can inform strategies to minimize ecological disruption and promote coexistence between human activities and marine life.  \n\nThese applications collectively contribute to the long-term sustainability and resilience of marine ecosystems.', 'contexts': 'vity, human activity, etc. Analyzing and controlling these factors can prevent the harm caused by sea level rise to human life and natural ecology."}\n{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Does the development of marine big data technology help in the protection of the marine ecological environment?\\n", "output": "The development of marine big data technology contributes to the sustainable protection of the marine ecological environment. It enhances the level of marine ecological protection through methods such as monitoring marine pollutants, predicting marine climate changes, and assessing the state of marine ecology."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit a news report on the development of marine resources.", "output": "With the continuous advancement of technology, the exploitation and utilization of marine resources have gradually come into people\'s field of vision. Marine oil, marine wind energy, and marine aquaculture have become the key directions for development. At the same time, there is a need to strengthen the protection of marine resources to ensure their sustainable use."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Why are oceans primarily concentrated in the tropical marine areas of the equator?", "output": "The tropical marine regions are characterized by the highest radiation intensity from the atmosphere, abundant sunlight, high temperatures, low pressure, maximum heat transfer, and the highest surface temperatures of the ocean, making them the ocean\'s heat storage areas."}\n', 'reference': 'Ocean big data technology can monitor and analyze multiple aspects of the marine environment, ecology, climate, resources, etc. It helps to identify problems and resolve them promptly, thereby protecting and managing marine resources. In addition, ocean big data technology can also provide guidance and support for the development of the marine industry.'}{'question': 'Identify the mineral resources in the east china sea area.', 'answer': '\n\nThe mineral resources in the East China Sea area include **oil, natural gas, coal, iron ore, manganese ore, tungsten ore, copper ore, gold ore, and silver ore**. Among these, **oil and natural gas** are the most significant, primarily located in regions such as the Yangtze River estuary basin, Zhejiang Taizhou basin, and Fujian basin. Coal and iron ore are mainly found in areas like Zhejiang and Fujian. Other minerals (e.g., manganese, tungsten, copper, gold, and silver ores) are widely distributed but face higher mining challenges.', 'contexts': 'intainability needs to be considered, in order to preserve the balance of marine ecology and prevent over-exploitation or destruction of resources."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "List the types of mineral resources in the East China Sea area.", "output": "The mineral resources in the East China Sea mainly include oil, natural gas, coal, iron ore, manganese ore, tungsten ore, copper ore, gold ore, silver ore, etc. Among them, oil and natural gas are the most important mineral resources in the East China Sea, mainly distributed in areas such as the Yangtze River estuary basin, Zhejiang Taizhou basin, Fujian basin, etc. Coal, iron ore and other mineral resources are mainly distributed in regions like Zhejiang, Fujian, etc. The distribution of manganese ore, tungsten ore, copper ore, gold ore, silver ore and other mineral resources is wide, but the difficulty of mining is relatively high."}{"task_type": "Analysis", "input": "Analyze the temperature changes in the beihai sea area over the past 7 days.", "output": "In the recent 7 days, the temperature in the Beihai sea area has dropped in a ring comparison, fluctuating from 28℃ to around 24℃."}\n', 'reference': 'The mineral resources in the East China Sea area mainly include natural gas, petroleum, coal, salt, phosphorite, etc.'}{'question': 'Recommend a type of submarine optical cable suitable for use in the east sea area.', 'answer': '\n\nBased on the context, if the requirement is for submarine optical cable in the East China Sea area, a **broadband optical fiber cable** is recommended for telecommunications transmission. This type of cable provides high bandwidth and strong anti-interference capabilities, making it suitable for reliable data and communication needs in marine environments. If combined power and data transmission are required, an electro-optic hybrid cable could also be considered.', 'contexts': 'ization is heading towards sustainable use and multi-faceted joint development, such as solar energy, seabed minerals, marine pharmaceuticals, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "If there is a need to lay new submarine cables in the East China Sea, what type of cable would you recommend?", "output": "Different types of submarine cables can be selected according to different needs. If it\'s used for power transmission, a high-voltage cable can be chosen; if it\'s for telecommunication transmission, a broadband optical fiber cable can be selected; if it\'s for alternating uses, a mixed cable can be picked. Considering comprehensively, we recommend choosing a electro-optic combined submarine cable, which has excellent features including high bandwidth and strong anti-interference ability."}{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Determine whether merchant ships near the east sea area have been attacked by pirates.", "output": "At present, no reports have been received about merchant ships in the East China Sea being attacked by pirates. However, this marine area remains in a high-risk zone. Thus, ships should strengthen their security measures and closely monitor the safety situation."}\n', 'reference': 'Based on your needs, I recommend using the certain model of submarine optic cable produced by a certain company. This optic cable uses a certain technology, which features a high transmission rate and stability, making it suitable for use in the East China Sea.'}{'question': 'Discussing how to improve maritime safety through technological means.', 'answer': '\n\nTo improve maritime safety through technological means, the following approaches can be considered based on the provided context:  \n\n1. **Enhanced Monitoring Technologies**:  \n   - **Remote Sensing and Satellite Technology**: These tools can monitor hazardous shipping routes, detect oil spills, and track weather patterns that impact safety. For example, satellite remote sensing provides real-time data on environmental conditions, helping vessels avoid high-risk areas.  \n   - **Hydroacoustic Technology**: This can be used to assess underwater hazards, such as submerged obstacles or shifts in ocean currents, improving navigational accuracy.  \n\n2. **Data-Driven Solutions**:  \n   - Analyzing marine accident data (as highlighted in the traffic safety summary) can identify recurring risks like overloading or meteorological factors. Integrating this with AI or predictive analytics could enable proactive risk mitigation.  \n\n3. **Future Innovations**:  \n   - The context emphasizes the need to "strengthen the innovation of monitoring methods" and improve accuracy. This could involve developing hybrid systems combining aerial drones, satellites, and IoT sensors for comprehensive, real-time monitoring.  \n\n4. **Environmental Adaptability**:  \n   - Strengthening governance and protection measures (as mentioned in the sustainable development context) can reduce pollution-related risks (e.g., oil spills) that endanger maritime operations.  \n\nBy leveraging these technologies and fostering innovation, maritime safety can be significantly enhanced while addressing environmental and operational challenges.', 'contexts': ' To achieve sustainable development of the oceans, it is necessary to strengthen protection and governance, and enhance environmental adaptability."}\n{"task_type": "Other", "input": "Write an article introducing marine pollution monitoring, including the monitoring scope, commonly used methods, and future development trends.", "output": "The scope of marine pollution monitoring includes marine sewage, solid waste, oil spills at sea, etc. Common methods include aerial remote sensing, hydroacoustic technology, satellite remote sensing, etc. The future development trend is to strengthen the innovation of monitoring methods and improve the accuracy of monitoring."}{"task_type": "Summary", "input": "Write an article on maritime traffic safety based on the marine accident data from the past year.", "output": "In recent years, maritime accidents have shown a continuous decline, yet they still occur occasionally. This article analyzes marine accident data from the last year, focusing particularly on hazardous shipping routes, ship overloading, and meteorological conditions that impact maritime safety. It also proposes corresponding solutions."}\n', 'reference': 'Improving the safety of maritime navigation can be approached from multiple aspects, such as improving the navigation system, strengthening communication and monitoring, etc. We need to continually research, optimize and enhance various technical measures.'}{'question': 'What is marine forecasting?', 'answer': '\n\nMarine forecasting is the process of predicting future weather and environmental conditions over the ocean. It involves analyzing environmental and physical processes, combining meteorology and computer technology to establish mathematical models. Common methods include **numerical forecasting**, which uses high-speed computer simulations to predict weather changes, and **expert forecasting**, which relies on manual observations and experienced analysis to anticipate trends. This helps support activities like fishing, navigation, and maritime safety by providing insights into factors such as wind, waves, temperature, and storms.', 'contexts': 'ne of China\'s important fishing bases, endowed with a wealth of fishery resources, including a variety of fish, shrimp, shellfish, and many others."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "How to predict the future weather of the ocean?", "output": "Predicting future marine weather requires an analysis of environmental and physical processes, combined with meteorology and computer technology, to establish mathematical forecast models and predict future trends. Common forecast methods include numerical forecasting and expert forecasting. Numerical forecasting simulates future weather changes through high-speed computer calculations, while expert forecasting predicts through manual observation and experience analysis."}{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Translate the following sentence into English: \\nDescribe the characteristics and lifestyle of a deep-sea creature.", "output": "Deep-sea creatures refer to organisms that live at depths exceeding 200 meters beneath the sea surface. They generally possess the ability to adapt to unique conditions such as high pressure, low temperatures, darkness, and lack of oxygen. Examples include the Deep-sea jellyfish, codfish, and sea cucumber, which predominantly inhabit cold, high-pressure deep waters and feed on other small marine life."}\n', 'reference': 'Marine forecasting refers to the real-time, accurate monitoring and predicting of oceanographic information such as meteorology, climate, hydrology, hydrodynamics, and waves through various technological methods, as well as the assessment and prediction of related impacts. Marine forecasting plays a very important role in offshore operations, marine development, and other aspects.'}{'question': 'Identify what kind of mineral resources can potentially be produced on the seabed?', 'answer': '\n\nBased on the provided context, the following mineral resources can potentially be produced on the seabed:  \n1. **Hydrothermal mineralization** (e.g., sulfide deposits rich in metals like copper, zinc, and gold).  \n2. **Manganese nodule-rich deposits** (concentrations of polymetallic nodules containing manganese, nickel, cobalt, and other metals).  \n3. **Deep-sea kaolin resources** (clay minerals with industrial applications).  \n\nThese are explicitly mentioned in the context as examples of seabed mineral resources.', 'contexts': 'the submarine topography and rock types, including hydrothermal mineralization, manganese nodule-rich deposits, and deep-sea kaolin resources, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "What technologies are used for detecting undersea mineral deposits? Which technology do you think has a better development prospect?", "output": "The current technologies for exploring seafloor mineral resources primarily include acoustic detection, electromagnetic detection, undersea drilling, and remote sensing technology. Among them, electromagnetic detection and remote sensing technology have broader development prospects, capable of identifying and locating mineral resources with higher precision and over a larger range."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Revise the following sentence: the development of seabed minerals is the main direction of current marine resources.", "output": "Underwater mineral resources are one of the significant areas in the current development of marine resources."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why do ships emit black smoke before entering the harbor?", "output": "Ships usually approach the corresponding area of a port before entering the harbor, then slow down and emit black smoke. This is a signal that can be detected by the ship\'s own equipment, and through this method, the port management department can prepare in advance for reception and operation."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Rank the following marine life according to the value of their feed from high to low: kelp, seaweed, sea urchin.", "output": "Sea urchin > Seaweed > Kelp."}