 Regular maintenance ensures the normal operation of submarine cables and guarantees the transmission quality of communication and power."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why is the speed of undersea cables slower than that of terrestrial fiber-optic cables?", "output": "Due to the uniqueness of the marine environment, submarine cables need to follow longer routes to complete data transmission. At the same time, the marine environment is relatively complex. Factors such as ocean currents and water pressure can cause certain disturbances to submarine cables, thereby affecting the speed and stability of signal transmission. Therefore, the transmission speed of submarine cables is often slower than that of terrestrial optical cables."}\n', 'reference': 'The repair of undersea cable faults requires a significant amount of time and resources, primarily due to the complexity of the underwater environment, high water pressure, and seawater corrosion, all of which significantly increase the difficulty of repairs.'}{'question': 'Describe the distribution of submarine cables in the east china sea area.', 'answer': '\n\nThe distribution of submarine cables in the East China Sea area includes communication and power cables from countries such as Japan, Korea, and China. These cables are primarily laid in a horizontal pattern, concentrated in the southern part of the East China Sea and extending north and south through the Yellow Sea region. This layout emphasizes the need for timely maintenance to ensure uninterrupted communication and power supply in the area. \n\n(Source: Task-type "Description" in the provided context)', 'contexts': ' are typically categorized into tropical depressions, tropical storms, typhoons, and super typhoons, etc., based on their wind speed and intensity."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the existing layout and distribution of submarine cables in the east china sea area.", "output": "Currently, there are multiple sub