nhance the ability to analyze complex, multidimensional data across marine, aerial, and spatial domains.', 'contexts': 'term for large-scale circulations of seawater, which are formed by the combined effects of tides, wind, gravity differences, and seabed topography."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the implementation principle of the air-space-sea three-dimensional perception technology.", "output": "The three-dimensional perception technology of space-air-sea, through the fusion of multi-source information and the combination of multi-energy level remote sensing data, obtains three-dimensional information of space, air, and sea, ultimately achieving comprehensive perception of the marine ecological environment."}{"task_type": "Summary", "input": "A certain research institution has recently released results pertaining to innovative oceanic robots.", "output": "A certain research institution has recently released the results of innovative marine robots. The robots can carry out long-term underwater exploration and monitoring, while also achieving real-time sensitive control. This provides a strong support for the development of the marine engineering field and deep-sea exploration."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract the latest article in the field of marine biology from the \\"science\\" magazine.", "output": "The latest issue of the \\"Science\\" magazine published a study called \\"Mapping the global threat of land-based marine pollution\\". Researchers used a new model to quantify the threat of land-based pollutants to marine biodiversity on a global scale."}\n', 'reference': 'Technologies such as domain-adaptive intelligent computing, machine learning, and deep learning have been widely used for comprehensive analysis of multidimensional data in marine, sky, and air, aiming to improve data processing speed and accuracy.'}{'question': 'What is a tropical cyclone? What kind of meteorological disasters can it cause?', 'answer': '\n\n