able use of resources."}\n{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify which mineral resources in the East China Sea area are worth collecting.", "output": "In the East China Sea region, there are abundant mineral resources, mainly including oil, natural gas, manganese, iron, aluminum, nickel, zinc and other metal deposits, as well as production and manufacturing raw materials such as phosphate and borax."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit a news report concerning the management of maritime traffic in the east china sea.", "output": "In recent years, the increase in marine traffic in the East China Sea has put significant pressure on maritime traffic management. To strengthen maritime traffic management, relevant departments in the region of the East China Sea have taken a series of measures, such as strengthening maritime patrols, improving navigation rules, and enhancing ship safety technologies. The implementation of these measures has effectively improved the maritime traffic safety level in the East China Sea, ensuring the smooth and secure maritime traffic."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Predicting the future development trends of marine energy generation technology.", "output": "Future marine energy generation technology will focus on improving energy utilization efficiency, reducing investment costs, and protecting the ecological environment. Meanwhile, the degree of intelligence and automation of power generation equipment will gradually improve; the research and application of new energy materials will provide more developmental opportunities for marine energy technology."}\n', 'reference': 'The recent mineral resource survey in the East China Sea area mainly includes phosphorus, natural gas, oil fields, manganese, etc. Due to the technical limitations in the oil and natural gas fields and the restrictions of related regulations, the excavation and utilization of the East China Sea area still need to be further developed. At t