, glacier melting, and factors such as increasing ocean temperatures and ocean expansion. All these factors have contributed to the rise in sea levels."}\n', 'reference': 'Offshore oil refers to the petroleum resources located in the ocean, which are typically included in sedimentary rock layers. The exploration and development of offshore oil is challenging, but as onshore oil resources gradually deplete, the value of its development is becoming increasingly important.'}{'question': 'Write a letter to a certain city government, suggesting the development of marine energy in the local area.', 'answer': '\n\n**Dear [City Government Leadership]:**  \n\nI am writing to propose the development of marine energy in our local area as a strategic initiative to advance sustainable growth, economic resilience, and environmental stewardship. Drawing on existing frameworks and best practices, I recommend the following measures:  \n\n1. **Policy Support and Regulatory Frameworks**  \n   - Establish clear policies and incentives (e.g., subsidies, tax breaks) to encourage investment in marine energy technologies such as tidal, wave, and offshore wind power.  \n   - Align local regulations with international standards, including the *United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea* and other relevant agreements, to ensure legal compliance and environmental protection.  \n\n2. **Technological Innovation and R&D**  \n   - Invest in research institutions and partnerships with universities to develop cutting-edge marine energy technologies tailored to our region’s unique conditions.  \n   - Facilitate collaboration with global experts to adopt advanced overseas technologies and foster innovation in energy efficiency and grid integration.  \n\n3. **Capital and Industry Collaboration**  \n   - Attract private and public funding by creating dedicated marine energy funds or green bonds.  \n   - Encourage partnerships between local businesses, international investors, and research organizations to scale up projects and reduce costs.  \n\n4. **Environmental and Security Safeguards**  \n   - Conduct rigorous environmental impact assessments to ensure marine energy projects coexist with biodiversity conservation.  \n   - Strengthen maritime law enforcement to prevent illegal activities (e.g., smuggling, unauthorized fishing) that could undermine energy infrastructure and ecological balance.  \n\nBy prioritizing marine energy, our city can position itself as a leader in the green economy while addressing climate challenges. I urge the leadership to consider these recommendations and take proactive steps to realize this transformative potential.  \n\nSincerely,  \n[Your Name/Title]  \n\n---  \n*Note: Adjust bracketed placeholders (e.g., city name, title) to personalize the letter.*', 'contexts': 'y undermines maritime security and national interests, demanding reinforced maritime law enforcement to crack down on illegal smuggling activities."}\n{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter to the relevant leaders, suggesting how to promote the development of the marine green industry.", "output": "Dear Leader: I believe that promoting the development of the marine green industry requires multi-faceted efforts such as strengthening policy support, promoting technological innovation, and introducing capital support. Specific recommendations include increasing investment in marine environmental protection, strengthening marine scientific and technological innovation, and introducing overseas technology and capital. We hope that the leadership can pay attention to and adopt our suggestions to promote the healthy development of the marine green industry."}{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What are the main international conventions in maritime laws and regulations?", "output": "\\"The United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea\\", \\"The International Convention on Civil Liability for Oil Pollution Damage\\", and \\"The International