r illegal dumping of plastics and chemicals, and mandate the use of cetacean-friendly fishing gear to reduce accidental bycatch.  \n3. **Enhance Monitoring and Enforcement**: Establish dedicated marine patrols (as outlined in standard protocols, e.g., life jackets, communication systems, and adherence to safety procedures) to monitor cetacean populations, deter poaching, and respond to strandings or distress calls.  \n4. **Invest in Scientific Research**: Allocate funding for studies on cetacean behavior, migration patterns, and the impacts of climate change, ensuring evidence-based policy-making.  \n5. **Promote Public Awareness and Collaboration**: Engage local communities, industries, and international partners in conservation efforts, emphasizing sustainable practices and the economic value of ecotourism centered on cetaceans.  \n\nMarine cetaceans—whales, dolphins, and porpoises—are not only ecological keystones but also cultural and economic assets. Their decline signals broader ecosystem collapse, with cascading effects on fisheries, tourism, and climate resilience. By prioritizing their protection, we align with global sustainability goals and demonstrate leadership in ocean stewardship.  \n\nWe urge your department to take urgent, measurable steps to reinforce legal frameworks, increase resource allocation, and collaborate with conservation experts. The time to act is now, before irreversible damage occurs.  \n\nThank you for your attention to this critical matter. We stand ready to support this cause through partnerships, data sharing, and advocacy.  \n\nSincerely,  \n[Your Full Name]  \n[Your Title/Organization Name]  \n[Contact Information]  \n\n---  \n*Note: Customize bracketed sections with specific details before sending.*', 'contexts': 'act the name of the largest species of deep-sea organisms.", "output": "It is also the largest fish species in the world, known as the whale shark."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Establish five requirements for