d habitat destruction, which disrupt breeding grounds.  \n\nProtecting the marine environment, enforcing sustainable fishing regulations, and mitigating pollution are critical to preserving fish resources in the region.', 'contexts': 'pment of the marine ecological environment; detecting, observing and predicting marine disasters to improve marine safety and service quality, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What factors affect the fishery resources in the East China Sea?", "output": "The fish resources in the East China Sea are affected by a variety of factors. These include marine environmental factors (such as water temperature, salinity, water quality, etc.), climate change, fishing activities, marine pollution etc. These factors can directly or indirectly affect the survival, reproduction and migration of fish, impacting the quantity and quality of fish resources. Protecting the marine environment and appropriately managing fisheries are important measures to protect fish resources."}{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify the main islands in the east china sea.", "output": "The main islands in the East Sea region include the Zhoushan Islands in Zhejiang, the Putian Archipelago in Fujian, the Xiangshan Archipelago in Zhejiang, the Shengsi Archipelago in Zhejiang, the Dinghai Archipelago in Zhejiang, Mount Putuo in Zhejiang, etc. Among them, the Zhoushan Islands in Zhejiang is the largest island group in the East Sea region, which is under the jurisdiction of Zhoushan City."}\n', 'reference': 'The fish resources in the East China Sea are affected by various factors, including overfishing, environmental pollution, climate change, etc. Overfishing can lead to a decrease in fish resources, environmental pollution can affect the growth and reproduction of fish, and climate change can also impact the ecological environment of fish. In order to ensure the sustainable use of fish resources in the East China Sea, it is necessary to strengthen