ost common fish in the East China Sea and is known for its delicious taste and rich nutrition."}\n{"task_type": "Analysis", "input": "Analyze the current situation of oil and gas resource development in the east china sea area.", "output": "The East China Sea is one of the most important offshore oil and gas resource development areas in China. However, the complexity of the marine environment and the high financial costs have limited the speed and scale of oil and gas exploration. In recent years, although China National Offshore Oil Corporation has been increasing its exploration efforts in the East China Sea, there have been relatively few significant oil and gas discoveries. In addition, research on the continuity of oil and gas resources in the East China Sea and the efficiency of mining still needs to be improved and perfected. In the future, we hope to increase investment in scientific research, improve exploration technologies and management levels, to ensure the sustainable development of oil and gas resources in the East China Sea to the greatest extent possible."}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Classify the following marine life: seahorses, corals, green sea turtles, starfish.", "output": "Seahorses and green sea turtles belong to vertebrates, while corals and starfish belong to invertebrates."}\n', 'reference': 'The yellow croaker in the East China Sea belongs to the order Perciformes, family Sciaenidae, genus Pseudosciaena, and is one of the important economic fish species in the East China Sea, distributed in the middle and upper waters of the sea area.'}{'question': 'Why are there many mineral resources in the East China Sea area?', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain information explaining why there are many mineral resources in the East China Sea area. While the context confirms the presence of significant metal mineral resources (e.g., copper, aluminum, zinc, lead) and their strategic importance to China's economy, it does not pr