ths, such as Mackerel, Shark, and Marlin.  \n3. **Deep-sea fish**: Inhabit deeper, darker waters and include species like Cod, Ray, and certain deep-sea Shark varieties.  \n\nThis classification is based on their habitat preferences and ecological adaptations.', 'contexts': ' etc. depending on shape and size. Different lifestyle habits and nutrition lead to separation into categories such as herbivorous and carnivorous."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Could you please categorize the fish resources in the East Sea according to their living habits?", "output": "The fish resources in the East China Sea can be classified according to their living habits into coastal fish, mid-depth fish, and deep-sea fish. Coastal fish include Yellow Croaker, Pomfret, and Crucian Carp; mid-depth fish include Mackerel, Shark, and Marlin; deep-sea fish include Cod, Ray, and Shark."}{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "Convert the ocean kinetic power into electrical energy output.", "output": "The natural forces such as wind, water flow, and tides at sea drive the rotation of the turbine. Then, the generator converts mechanical energy into electrical energy, which is finally output through the transmission line."}\n{"task_type": "Analysis", "input": "Analyze how the underwater mineral resources are distributed.", "output": "The areas with a dense distribution of underwater mineral resources are mainly located in the Pacific, Atlantic, and Indian Oceans."}\n', 'reference': 'The fish resources in the East China Sea can be classified according to their habits as benthic fish, mid-water fish, and upper layer fish.'}{'question': 'Recommend a multibeam depth sounder suitable for seafloor topography measurement.', 'answer': '\n\nIt is recommended to use a multibeam echo sounder for seafloor topography measurement. This instrument is specifically designed to provide high-resolution depth and topographic data by emitting multiple sound beams simultaneously, making it ideal for detailed underwater mapping. \n\n(Source: Context includes a prior recommendation for a multibeam echo sounder for depth and topography measurements.)', 'contexts': 'd emergency response, reinforcing cable protection, guardianship, and other coordinated work, to ensure the safe operation of the submarine cables."}\n{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "Recommend an instrument that can measure the depth and topography of seawater.", "output": "It is recommended to use a multibeam echo sounder for depth and topography measurements."}{"task_type": "Analysis", "input": "Analyze the reasons and impacts of the overexploitation of inshore fishery resources.", "output": "Overfishing and evident over-exploitation of resources are the main causes for the decline in offshore fishery resources. This situation not only leads to a reduction in fishery production value, but also has a negative impact on the overall aquatic ecological environment, causing problems such as a decrease in marine species diversity and an imbalance in the marine ecology."}\n{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "Convert the length of the natural gas pipeline in the east china sea area into kilometers.", "output": "The length of the natural gas pipeline in the East China Sea area is approximately 500 kilometers."}\n', 'reference': 'The EM2040C multibeam depth sounder produced by Kongsberg company can be widely used in many fields including seafloor topography measurement and underwater measurement. It is also applicable in technical fields such as underwater work robots and remote sensing measurement. With powerful features such as real-time processing and data transmission, it boasts a high level of accuracy.'}{'question': 'Briefly describe the impact of typhoons on marine environment and ecology.', 'answer': '\n\nThe impact of typhoons on the marine environment and ecology includes physical disturbances such as strong winds, storm surges, and large waves, which can disrupt marine habitats, damage coral reefs, and alter sediment distribution. These extreme conditions may also affect marine biodiversity by displacing species or altering their ecosystems. Additionally, typhoons can influence water quality through increased runoff and turbulence, potentially leading to short-term ecological stress. The provided context emphasizes the necessity of scientific management and protection measures to mitigate these impacts and ensure sustainable marine resource conservation.', 'contexts': 't will have certain impacts on the marine ecological environment, thus necessitating the adoption of scientific management and protection measures."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Title: An Investigation Report on Marine Research\\n\\nAbstract: This report provides an in-depth analysis of our recent investigation into marine ecosystems. Covering diverse key aspects such as biodiversity, water quality, and the impact of climate change, the report serves to highlight our scientific findings, potential challenges, and subsequent recommendations to promote the sustainable management and conservation of marine resources.", "output": "Title: \\"Oceanographic Report: Unveiling the Mysteries of the South China Sea Deep-Sea Ecosystem.\\" \\n\\nAbstract: This report focuses on the South China Sea deep-sea as the subject of research, revealing the rare living creatures in the deep-sea environment and their adaptations. The research findings will have significant implications for biodiversity conservation and marine environmental governance."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Why does a typhoon cause strong winds and huge waves?", "output": "Typhoons inherently come with extreme wind force and storm surges, and they are affected by various factors such as terrain, ocean temperature, and atmospheric pressure. This often leads to strong winds and large waves, posing significant hazards and impacts on marine navigation and coastal areas."}\n', 'reference': 'Typhoons not only cause damage to the marine ecological environment, but also lead to losses of marine resources. This includes declining marine life catch and fishing industry losses, etc. In addition, typhoons can also lead to water quality degradation, marine pollution, and coastal land subsidence problems.'}{'question': 'Convert the following latitude and longitude coordinates into the commonly used format: (48.8798° n, 2.3530° e).', 'answer': '\n\nThe commonly used format for the coordinates (48.8798° N, 2.3530° E) is **48°52\'47.28" N, 2°21\'10.8" E** (degrees, minutes, seconds). \n\nThis is derived by converting the decimal degrees to the DMS format:  \n- **Latitude**: 48.8798° = 48° + (0.8798 × 60) = 48°52.788\' = 48°52\' + (0.788 × 60) ≈ 48°52\'47.28".  \n- **Longitude**: 2.3530° = 2° + (0.3530 × 60) = 2°21.18\' = 2°21\' + (0.18 × 60) ≈ 2°21\'10.8".  \n\nIf you need further clarification, let me know!', 'contexts': 'ion, there are some transnational submarine cables in the East China Sea, connecting countries and regions including China, Japan, and South Korea."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the reasons for the formation of ocean surface currents.", "output": "The surface currents of the ocean are primarily formed by the combined effects of the Coriolis force caused by the Earth\'s rotation and factors such as wind."}{"task_type": "Transformation", "input": "Translate the coordinates of the maritime search and rescue team on the nautical chart into longitude and latitude coordinates.", "output": "The search and rescue team is located on the nautical map at coordinates X=785.6km, Y=588km, which translates into longitude coordinates of 116.4 degrees and latitude coordinates of 31.3 degrees."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Write a promotional script to popularize ocean conservation knowledge among the public.", "output": "In order to protect our marine environment, each of us should have a sense of environmental protection. Starting from protecting every marine life, we should produce less garbage and focus more on recycling. We should actively participate in public welfare activities such as beach cleaning and environmental protection actions, collectively contributing our time and effort towards the protection of the ocean."}\n', 'reference': '(48°52\'47.28" N, 2°21\'10.8" E).'}{'question': 'What are the undersea cables in the East China Sea mainly used for?', 'answer': '\n\nThe undersea cables in the East China Sea are primarily used for **information transmission and power supply**. For information transmission, they serve as critical infrastructure for international internet connectivity, supporting global communication, data exchange, and financial systems. For power supply, they transport resources like oil and natural gas to offshore platforms and provide electricity to marine facilities, contributing to national economic security. \n\nThis information is derived from the provided context.', 'contexts': 'gy, the use of materials is very extensive, including construction materials, coating materials, solar energy materials, wind power materials, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Briefly introduce the main uses of the subsea cables in the east sea area.", "output": "The main purposes of the undersea cables in the East China Sea are information transmission and power supply. In terms of information, undersea cables are an important method for international internet access, providing vital support for the fields of international communication, data transmission, finance, etc. In terms of power supply, undersea cables are used to deliver resources such as oil and natural gas to offshore platforms, and to meet the power needs of related facilities, playing a significant role in ensuring national economic security."}{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter inviting the vessels conducting scientific surveys in the east sea to attend the international marine science research conference.", "output": "I have prepared a letter for you, inviting ships conducting scientific research in the East China Sea to participate in the International Ocean Science Research Conference. The letter contains information such as the conference\'s time, location, and agenda."}\n', 'reference': 'The undersea cables in the East China Sea area are mainly used for communication and power transmission.'}{'question': 'What is the main use of the undersea cables in the East Sea area?', 'answer': '\n\nThe main uses of the undersea cables in the East Sea area are **information transmission** and **power supply**. For information transmission, they facilitate international internet access, supporting global communication, data exchange, and financial systems. For power supply, they transport resources like oil and natural gas to offshore platforms and provide electricity to marine facilities, contributing to national economic security. \n\n(Source: Provided context)', 'contexts': 'gy, the use of materials is very extensive, including construction materials, coating materials, solar energy materials, wind power materials, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Briefly introduce the main uses of the subsea cables in the east sea area.", "output": "The main purposes of the undersea cables in the East China Sea are information transmission and power supply. In terms of information, undersea cables are an important method for international internet access, providing vital support for the fields of international communication, data transmission, finance, etc. In terms of power supply, undersea cables are used to deliver resources such as oil and natural gas to offshore platforms, and to meet the power needs of related facilities, playing a significant role in ensuring national economic security."}{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter inviting the vessels conducting scientific surveys in the east sea to attend the international marine science research conference.", "output": "I have prepared a letter for you, inviting ships conducting scientific research in the East China Sea to participate in the International Ocean Science Research Conference. The letter contains information such as the conference\'s time, location, and agenda."}\n', 'reference': 'The undersea cables in the East China Sea are primarily used for communication and internet transmission. The construction and operation of these cables play a significant role in promoting economic development and information exchange in the East China Sea region.'}{'question': 'Describe the characteristics of the fishery resources in the east sea area?', 'answer': "\n\nThe fishery resources in the East Sea area are characterized by a diverse range of species and distinct distribution patterns. Key resources include **hairtail, herring, cutlassfish, cod, scallops, and seaweed**. These are predominantly found in **coastal and shallower sea areas**, with hairtail, herring, and cutlassfish being the most abundant and commonly consumed fish species. Cod, however, is less widespread and typically inhabits regions with lower salinity. Scallops and seaweed thrive in shallower waters. The distribution and quantity of these resources are influenced by factors such as **ocean currents, climate conditions, and human activities**. This variability highlights the dynamic nature of the East Sea's marine ecosystem and its susceptibility to environmental and anthropogenic changes.", 'contexts': 'tc. By exploiting and utilizing island resources, it is possible to effectively expand the economic activities and innovation ability of the region."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the major fish resources and their distribution in the east sea region.", "output": "The East Sea region\'s primary fish resources include hairtail, herring, cutlassfish, cod, scallops, and seaweed. They are widely distributed and mainly congregated in the coastal sea areas. Hairtail, herring, and cutlassfish are the most common edible fish species in the East Sea region and are quite abundant. Cod, on the other hand, is found in areas with lower salinity and is relatively less distributed. Scallops and seaweed are primarily found in the shallower sea areas. The quantity and distribution of fish resources may vary due to factors such as regional currents, climate, and human activities."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Briefly describe the application scope of ocean satellite remote sensing technology.", "output": "Ocean satellite remote sensing technology can be applied to numerous fields including marine meteorology, marine environment, marine resources, and marine transportation. It enables high-precision remote sensing observation of the marine environment, offering all-weather, multi-angle ocean observation. This technology can detect information such as ocean surface wave height, water depth, marine climate, and sea ice distribution."}\n', 'reference': 'The fish resources in the East China Sea area are characterized by diversity and abundance. Among them, the number of inshore fish is more, and the species are also relatively abundant, mainly distributed in the shallow sea areas; the number of mid-water fish is less, and the species are relatively less, mainly distributed in the deep sea areas; the number of deep-sea fish is less, and the species are relatively singular, mainly distributed in the deep sea areas.'}{'question': 'Recommend a space-air-sea three-dimensional perception application that can enhance the economic benefits of ocean economy.', 'answer': '\n\n**Recommendation:**  \nA **Space-Air-Sea Integrated Resource Monitoring and Management System** could significantly enhance the economic benefits of the ocean economy. This application combines satellite remote sensing (space), aerial drones (air), and underwater sensors/autonomous vehicles (sea) to create a real-time, three-dimensional perception network.  \n\n**Key Features and Benefits:**  \n1. **Resource Exploration & Optimization:**  \n   - Use satellite imagery and AI to map mineral-rich zones (e.g., gold, copper, petroleum) in the Philippine Sea, guiding targeted extraction efforts.  \n   - Drones and underwater robots can assess resource quantities and environmental conditions, reducing exploration costs and improving efficiency.  \n\n2. **Smart Fisheries & Aquaculture:**  \n   - Monitor ocean temperatures, currents, and plankton levels (via satellites and underwater sensors) to optimize fishery yields and aquaculture practices.  \n   - Predict fish migration patterns to enhance catch rates while avoiding overfishing.  \n\n3. **Marine Logistics & Safety:**  \n   - Track shipping routes in real time using aerial and satellite data to avoid hazards, reduce fuel consumption, and lower operational risks.  \n   - Enhance disaster response (e.g., oil spills, typhoons) with rapid data collection and analysis from all three dimensions.  \n\n4. **Environmental Protection & Compliance:**  \n   - Monitor pollution levels and ecological changes to ensure sustainable resource use, aligning economic growth with environmental stewardship.  \n\nBy integrating space-air-sea perception, this system would boost resource utilization efficiency, reduce costs, and support data-driven decision-making, directly advancing the economic and ecological sustainability of maritime industries.', 'contexts': 'ilippine Sea is an area extremely rich in mineral resources, owning various minerals such as gold, silver, copper, iron, zinc, petroleum, and more."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Infer: what impact would the implementation of air-space-sea three-dimensional perception technology have on the advancement of national maritime economic development?", "output": "Implementing space-earth-sea three-dimensional perception technology can enable a country to monitor, identify, and utilize marine resources more effectively, thereby promoting the sus