stion': 'What are the main fields of application for marine big data technology?', 'answer': '\n\nThe main fields of application for marine big data technology include:  \n1. **Marine Resource Development**: Such as marine energy (offshore wind power, ocean thermal energy conversion, tidal energy, deep sea water utilization) to improve development efficiency and reliability.  \n2. **Marine Environment Protection and Management**: Utilizing data integration and analysis to monitor and manage ocean ecosystems, pollution, and climate impacts.  \n3. **Marine Ecological Monitoring**: Leveraging remote sensing technology to track ocean color, temperature, salinity, sea ice, and biological communities for ecological conservation.  \n4. **Marine Resource Surveys**: Supporting activities like fisheries management, mineral exploration, and habitat mapping through data-driven insights.  \n\nThese applications rely on technologies like remote sensing and big data analytics to address challenges in sustainability, energy, and environmental stewardship.', 'contexts': 'osystem. Its extensive application can guide the development of marine resources, marine environment protection and management, among other fields."}\n{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the application of marine big data technology in the field of marine energy.", "output": "The application of marine big data technology in the field of marine energy includes offshore wind power, ocean thermal energy conversion, tidal energy, deep sea water utilization, etc. Through the integration, analysis, and application of marine data, we can improve the development efficiency and reliability of marine energy."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the application of remote sensing technology in marine observation.", "output": "Remote sensing technology obtains various information about the ocean surface and underwater through high-altitude platforms such as satellites and airplanes, including physical quantities such as ocean color, temperature, salinity, suspended particle concentration, and sea surface height, as well as the distribution of elements such as sea ice, ocean meadows, and biological communities. These data can be used for ocean environmental monitoring, marine ecological protection, marine resource surveys, etc., and have significant application value."}\n', 'reference': 'The application fields of marine big data technology are very wide, including but not limited to the following aspects: marine ecosystem monitoring, marine weather forecasting, marine resource development, marine engineering simulation and emulation, marine safety guarantee, marine environmental protection and so on.'}{'question': 'What is the typical lifespan of undersea cables?', 'answer': '\n\nThe typical lifespan of undersea fiber optic cables is roughly over 20 years. However, this can vary depending on factors such as the quality of the cable, installation methods, underwater environmental conditions, and potential human-induced damage.', 'contexts': 's the marine environment divided into?", "output": "The marine environment can be divided into three types: beaches, nearshore, and open sea areas."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What is the lifespan of submarine optical cables?", "output": "The lifespan of undersea fiber optic cables is roughly over 20 years. However, the actual lifespan can be affected by various factors, including the quality of the cable, the installation method, the underwater environment, human damage, and so on."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit an article about the world\'s largest marine data sharing platform.", "output": "The largest global ocean data sharing platform is OOI, which provides real-time and historical ocean data to scientists and the public. It is the largest global ocean observation network after GOOS."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "May I ask, in the latest marine propulsion system products, which components play an important role in their performance?", "output": "In the latest marine propulsion system products, components such as engines, propellers, and rudders play a significant role in performance."}\n', 'reference': 'The lifespan of underwater cables is affected by various factors, such as the quality of cable material, seabed environments, and the degree of erosion by marine life. Generally, the service life of underwater cables is around 20 years. High-quality underwater cables can last even longer, up to 40 years. However, whether the cable lifespan can be extended requires regular inspection, maintenance, as well as confronting the damage caused by complex harsh environmental changes and human factors.'}{'question': 'Analyze the hydrological fluctuations caused by deep-sea waveguide.', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain information on the hydrological fluctuations caused by deep-sea waveguides. I don't know.", 'contexts': 'found in deep-sea basins, and they typically feature high density, high hardness, high specific gravity, and large depositional distribution areas."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Classify the ocean hydrodynamics methods into two types: measurement and numerical calculation.", "output": "The methods in ocean hydrodynamics include measurement methods and numerical calculation methods. The measurement methods, including empirical formulas and experimentation, can be used to measure information in the ocean such as current velocity, surge, and waves. The numerical calculation methods, which include the Lagrangian and Eulerian methods, can simulate dynamic phenomena in the ocean, predict natural phenomena, and provide information support for the utilization and management of marine resources."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Does the transmission rate of undersea optical cables get affected by the temperature of the seawater?", "output": "The transmission rate of undersea optical cables is affected by 