mendations beyond the provided context, the database does not contain additional information.', 'contexts': 'environment, prevent and reduce marine pollution, protect marine biological resources, and prevent the destruction of underwater cultural heritage."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "List a few commonly used marine environmental monitoring indicators.", "output": "Common indicators for marine environment monitoring include water temperature, salinity, dissolved oxygen, pH value, nutrients, and organic matter, etc."}{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "Recommend an application suitable for use during island vacations.", "output": "Island tourism has become one of the popular travel methods today, and SeaView is an app suitable for use on islands. SeaView has been widely used in over 250 countries and regions around the world, with the following features: Firstly, it is an app with a relatively rich channel, users can learn about various marine attractions such as underwater resources and beautiful scenery; Secondly, it has a convenient search function, which can efficiently retrieve relevant marine information according to different needs; Thirdly, it supports multiple language versions, thus it is convenient for foreign tourists to use; Fourthly, it has a comprehensive navigation function, which can help users understand their current location on the island better."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "What are the different types of ocean waves?", "output": "Common types of sea waves include aggressive destructive waves, wind waves that cause breaking waves, burning waves synchronized with the landform, and complex surging waves, etc."}\n', 'reference': "You can try downloading apps like 'Ocean Environment Monitor' and 'Blue Ocean'. They can supply you with information about the ocean environment, weather forecasts and more."}{'question': 'What are the purposes of the submarine cables in the East China Sea area?', 'answer': '\n\nThe submarine cables in the East China Sea serve several key purposes:  \n1. **Transnational Communication and Data Transmission**: They connect mainland China with Taiwan, Japan, and South Korea, facilitating cross-border communication and high-speed data exchange.  \n2. **Marine Observation and Research**: Used for monitoring oceanic conditions, exploring marine resources, and conducting undersea geological studies.  \n3. **Economic and Scientific Development**: Their stability and high-speed capabilities support regional economic growth and advance scientific research in marine fields.  \n\nThis information is derived from the provided context.', 'contexts': 's. In addition, the installation and maintenance of underwater cables require professional equipment and technicians, which also increase the cost."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Write an article about the submarine cables in the east sea area, introducing their importance and application fields.", "output": "Submarine cables in the East China Sea play an important role in modern communication and information transmission. They connect the mainland China with Taiwan region, mainland China with Japan, and mainland China with South Korea, etc., realizing transnational communication and data transmission. Submarine cables are also widely used in fields such as marine observation, marine resource exploration, and undersea geological research. Their stability and high-speed transmission capabilities are of vital significance for promoting regional economic development and scientific research."}{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Categorize the important seaports of our country into northern and southern ports.", "output": "Northern ports: Tianjin Port, Dalian Port, Qingdao Port; Southern ports: Shanghai Port, Shenzhen Port, Ningbo Port."}\n{"task_type": "Summary", "input": "Briefly outline the ecological conservation measures implemented in the marine environmental protection work.", "output": "Ecological conservation measures implemented in marine environmental protection work include: establishing protected areas, fishing restricted areas and marine parks; strengthening the protection of biodiversity such as coral reefs, seagrass, seabed hard bottom, wetlands, etc.; and enhancing the protection of wild flora and fauna."}\n', 'reference': 'The undersea cables in the East China Sea are primarily used for communication and internet transmission, enabling global communication and data transfer.'}{'question': 'What is the most common fish species in the East China Sea?', 'answer': '\n\nThe most common fish species in the East China Sea include yellow croaker, pomfret, sea bream, crucian carp, and eel, among others.', 'contexts': 'a?", "output": "The most common fish species in the East China Sea include yellow croaker, pomfret, sea bream, crucian carp, and eel, among others."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Edit an article introducing the submarine topography of the east china sea, requiring it to be accurate and easy to understand.", "output": "The seabed topography of the East China Sea is a diverse underwater terrain, characterized by its flat terrain, with striking features such as seabed hills and seamounts. Among them, seabed peaks, submarine canyons, submarine long mountains, seafloor depressions, and submarine rift valleys are all distributed. Researchers have conducted in-depth probes into the seabed topography in the East China Sea and found that it was formed millions of years ago by a series of natural forces such as earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, and geological movements. This is one of the important evidences of the evolution of the Earth\'s crust.\\n"}{"task_type": "Recommendation", "input": "Recommend a cultivation method for marine green resources.", "output": "It is recommended to adopt the cultivation of seawater rice, which reduces the reliance on freshwater resources and can effectively improve agricultural production benefits."}\n', 'reference': 