: "Help edit a review article on the detection of marine mineral resources.", "output": "The exploration of underwater mineral resources involves the use of scientific and technological means to probe minerals beneath the earth\'s surface. Currently, we mainly focus on mineral resources such as manganese nodules, sulfide ores, and hydrothermal minerals. Underwater mineral resources are one of the main focuses for future exploration. There are various detection methods, such as sonar, remote sensing, deep-sea robots, etc. As technology advances, these methods will become more accurate and efficient."}{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What is an ocean current? What are the classifications of ocean currents?", "output": "Ocean currents refer to the movement of water bodies exhibited in the ocean, in which the flow speed in the deep water is relatively slow, while it accelerates near the seabed. According to the modes of flow and the scope of impact, ocean currents can be divided into several categories such as tropical currents, marginal gyres, westerly drift, and antarctic circumpolar current."}\n', 'reference': 'High-resolution marine remote sensing technology can be used to discover resources such as oceanic sediments, paleontological fossils, and oil and gas.'}{'question': 'May I ask, which is the largest seaport in our country?', 'answer': "\n\nThe database does not contain information about the largest seaport in the country. I don't know the answer to this question.", 'contexts': 'thening scientific research efforts, and continuous improvement of technical means to ensure the sustainable development of marine green resources."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "May I ask, which is currently the largest cargo ship in the world?", "output": "The largest cargo ship in the world currently is the Ore Tianjin, built by the U.K., with a length of approximately 400 meters and a width of about 59 meters, capable of carrying 400,000 tons of ore."}