strictly in accordance with domestic regulations, ready to deal with any emergencies at all times, ensuring the safe and efficient completion of the project."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Can undersea cables self-repair?", "output": "Submarine cables do not possess the capability to self-repair. Damage to these cables requires manual repair and replacement, which typically necessitates professional technicians and equipment."}\n', 'reference': 'The basic components contained in submarine cables mainly include the cable core, insulation layer, shielding layer, sheath, etc. Among them, the cable core is the center for electrical signal transmission, the insulation layer primarily has insulating properties, the shielding layer is used to prevent environmental interference from affecting the signals, and the sheath serves a protective and maintenance role. These components all have specific technical requirements, and all play important roles in the lifespan of submarine cables and the quality of signal transmission.'}{'question': 'May I ask what islands are there in the East China Sea?', 'answer': "\n\nThe East China Sea is home to several islands, including **Diaoyu Island**, **Chiwei Island**, **Huangwei Island**, and the **Zhoushan Islands**. These islands are part of China's territory and hold significant strategic and economic value, particularly in tourism, fisheries, and marine energy. This information is based on the provided context.", 'contexts': 'certain results. At present, the island resources in the East China Sea area are mainly used in tourism, fisheries, marine energy and other fields."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Which islands are located in the East China Sea?", "output": "There are several islands in the East China Sea, including Diaoyu Island, Chiwei Island, Huangwei Island, Zhoushan Islands, etc. These islands are all part of our country\'s territory and have significant strategic and economic value."}{"task