ines are of significant importance in promoting the interconnection of energy and the development of information technology."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "What do you think is the future development trend of marine green resources?", "output": "The future development trend will focus more on ecology and environmental protection. In the process of developing and utilizing marine green resources, it is necessary to further strengthen the awareness of ecological ethics and deeply explore the types and values of marine green resources."}{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "Are there any dangerous areas in the shipping lanes of the East China Sea?", "output": "There are some dangerous areas in the shipping lanes of the East China Sea, such as shipwreck sites, shoals, and reefs. Ships need to avoid these hazards during their voyages to ensure their safety and smooth operation."}\n{"task_type": "Judgment", "input": "True or false? The impact of meteorites striking the ocean environment can last for decades or even centuries.", "output": "Indeed, the impact of meteorites on the ocean environment can generate effects similar to earthquakes and water waves. If the impact site is on the seashore or in the center of the ocean, it can affect the dynamics of the ocean for a considerable length of time and may also cause a series of man-made environmental problems."}\n', 'reference': 'In recent years, the green development of the ocean has become a global focus, with the main directions including marine ecological protection, clean marine energy, marine circular economy, and marine technology innovation, among others. The future of marine green development will continue to revolve around these key areas, and with the implementation of the "Belt and Road" initiative, it will be necessary to vigorously develop marine industries related to marine green development, creating more job opportunities and economic benefits for people.'}{'question': 'Has the undersea p