ingbo Port, Xiamen Port and so on. These ports not only offer docking services for cruise ships, but also provide various tourism and entertainment facilities for visitors.'}{'question': 'What mineral resources are found in the East China Sea area?', 'answer': '\n\nThe main mineral resources in the East China Sea include:  \n- **Fossil fuel resources**: Oil and gas, natural gas hydrates.  \n- **Biogenic mineral resources**: Phosphates, manganese nodules.  \n- **Metal mineral resources**: Iron ore, copper ore, metal sulfides.  \n\nThis information is derived from the provided context.', 'contexts': 'he research and development and advancement of submarine cable technology to adapt to the growing needs of undersea transmission and communication."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "List and categorize the main mineral resources in the east china sea area.", "output": "The main mineral resources in the East China Sea include oil and gas, natural gas hydrates, phosphates, manganese nodules, iron ore, copper ore, and metal sulfides. Among them, oil and gas and natural gas hydrates are categorized as fossil fuel resources, while phosphates and manganese nodules are categorized as biogenic mineral resources. Iron ore, copper ore, and metal sulfides are classified as metal mineral resources."}{"task_type": "Recognition", "input": "Identify the main seabed topographic features in the east china sea.", "output": "The main seabed topographic features in the East China Sea include seamounts, ocean trenches, oceanic ridges, and sea platforms, among others. Among them, the Huaniao Mountain submarine volcano is the most famous seabed topography in the East China Sea, and seamounts and oceanic ridges are the main features of the seabed topography. An ocean trench is one of the depths of the seabed topography, and the deepest trench in the East China Sea is the Ryukyu Trench, which reaches a depth of about 8,000 meters."}\n', 'reference': 'The mineral resources in the East Sea area mainly include iron ore, manganese ore, copper ore, gold ore, silver ore, etc. Among them, iron ore and manganese ore are the main mineral resources in the East Sea area, with a wide distribution.'}{'question': 'Why is the study of ocean power systems so important?', 'answer': '\n\nThe study of ocean power systems is important because the oceanic dynamic system plays a significant role in influencing global climate. Understanding these systems helps in analyzing marine environmental changes, improving climate model predictions, and advancing knowledge of global climate patterns and marine ecological interactions. This is critical for addressing challenges such as climate change, ecosystem preservation, and sustainable resource management.', 'contexts': 'e organic materials. Deep-sea hydrothermal vents have become a hot research topic in the fields of geology, chemistry, and biology in recent years."}\n{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "Explain the importance of understanding marine power systems for the study of marine science.", "output": "The oceanic dynamic system is a significant factor influencing the global climate. Understanding the oceanic dynamic system is beneficial for studying marine environmental changes, conducting climate model predictions, and presenting global climate and marine ecology, among other aspects."}{"task_type": "Description", "input": "Describe the situation of submarine cables in the east china sea area.", "output": "The submarine cables in the East China Sea are mainly used for communication and power transmission, including international submarine optical cables and domestic submarine electrical cables. Among them, the international submarine optical cables primarily connect China, Japan, Korea, Taiwan, and other countries and regions, while the domestic submarine electrical cables mainly connect various coastal provinces and cities in China. Due to the frequent earthquakes in the East China Sea, the maintenance and protection of submarine cables are very important."}\n', 'reference': 'The study of marine power systems is of great significance for understanding the characteristics of the marine environment, recognizing the composition and operational mechanisms of marine ecosystems, etc. It helps us to better maintain and protect the marine environment and promote sustainable development.'}{'question': 'Briefly explain the role of marine standardization.', 'answer': '\n\nMarine standardization plays a critical role in ensuring consistency, quality, and international alignment in marine activities. It involves establishing systematic frameworks, improving standard-setting mechanisms, and integrating advanced technologies and research to enhance the scientific rigor of marine practices. Additionally, it promotes public awareness and adoption of standards, facilitating collaboration and efficiency in fields like marine observation, resource management, and environmental protection.', 'contexts': 'ional instruments, CTD instruments, hydrogen-oxygen isotope instruments, submersibles, buoys, and automatic hydrological observation stations, etc."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Share your thoughts on how to promote the standardization of marine work.", "output": "To promote the standardization of marine work, it is necessary to strengthen the alignment with international standards, learn from advanced international experiences, and improve the related standard systems and standard-setting mechanisms. It is also essential to enhance technological research and development and cultivate talents, thereby increasing the scientific and normative nature of standard setting. Moreover, it is crucial to reinforce the promotion and publicity of standards, enhancing the social public\'s awareness of standards."}{"task_type": "Commonsense Reasoning", "input": "What is a black sand beach?", "output": "The black beach is mainly formed by the long-term erosion of sea winds and waves on black volcanic rocks erupted from nearby volcanic activities."}\n{"task_type": "Classification", "input": "Classify the following fish according to their living environment: striped marlin, seahorse, grouper, ricefish.", "output": "Marine fish: Mackerel, Seahorse, Grouper\\nFreshwater fish: Rice Field Fish"}\n', 'reference': 'Ocean standardization can provide scientific, reasonable, and fair standard criteria, which is beneficial for regulating various tasks in the ocean field. It helps promote the development and utilization of ocean resources, protect and govern the marine environment, and improve the level of marine economic and technological development.'}{'question': 'Edit an announcement about marine ecology protection.', 'answer': '\n\n**Announcement: Marine Ecology Protection Initiative**  \n\nTo safeguard our marine ecosystems and promote sustainable development, all participants in marine activities are required to adhere to the following guidelines:  \n\n1. **Safety First**: Mandatory use of life jackets and proper safety gear during all water-based operations.  \n2. **Resource Management**: Ensure adequate supplies and equipment are available to minimize environmental impact.  \n3. **Communication**: Maintain reliable communication systems to coordinate efforts and respond to emergencies.  \n4. **Environmental Monitoring**: Stay vigilant to weather changes, tides, and ocean conditions to avoid disruptions to marine life.  \n5. **Compliance**: Follow industry standards and operating procedures to protect biodiversity and prevent pollution.  \n\nAdditionally, we emphasize the importance of **protecting marine green resources** through responsible practices, advancing eco-friendly technologies, and supporting scientific research. Collaborative efforts are essential to preserve marine ecosystems for future generations.  \n\nFor inquiries or policy recommendations, contact the local marine conservation office.  \n\n---  \nThis draft integrates safety protocols, ecological considerations, and sustainable practices derived from the provided context. Let me know if further adjustments are needed!', 'contexts': 'act the name of the largest species of deep-sea organisms.", "output": "It is also the largest fish species in the world, known as the whale shark."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Establish five requirements for standard marine patrol.", "output": "1. Each participant must wear a life jacket; \\n2. There should be enough equipment and supplies during patrols; \\n3. There should be good communication protection during patrols; \\n4. Pay attention to meteorological changes and tides during patrols; \\n5. Strictly adhere to industry standards and operating procedures."}{"task_type": "Letter Writing", "input": "Write a letter to the local government, introducing your research findings to assist them in formulating more scientific marine conservation policies.", "output": "Dear leader, our research findings indicate that the stability of marine ecosystems is closely related to human life. We suggest strengthening marine environmental protection efforts, formulating more scientific ocean management policies, and increasing investment in marine scientific research to ensure the health and sustainable development of marine ecosystems."}\n{"task_type": "Open-ended Generation", "input": "Could you discuss the issues that need to be addressed in the development of marine green resources?", "output": "The following issues should be taken into consideration during the development of marine green resources: protecting the marine ecological environment, preventing marine pollution and depletion of marine biological resources; making rational use of marine green resources, promoting the upgrading of marine industries and sustainable development; strengthening the research and development and innovation of marine green technologies, to provide effective support for the development of marine green resources."}\n', 'ref