round the world, enabling a comprehensive monitoring and data collection of the marine environment."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "What are the conditions for the formation of a typhoon?", "output": "The formation of typhoons requires a combination of various factors, including suitable atmospheric conditions, warm and humid air currents, and the earth\'s rotation. Generally, tropical cyclones may evolve into typhoons when they encounter suitable meteorological conditions over tropical oceans."}\n', 'reference': 'The largest passenger ship in the East China Sea is a luxury cruise ship, approximately 300 meters long and 40 meters wide, capable of accommodating 5,000 passengers.'}{'question': 'Summarize the benefits of utilizing marine energy and its development trends.', 'answer': '\n\nThe benefits of marine energy include its renewability, stability, low carbon footprint, environmental friendliness, and wide geographic coverage. It can also be integrated with other energy sources to enhance energy supply stability and reliability.  \n\nDevelopment trends in marine energy focus on technological advancements, such as improving equipment durability and efficiency, optimizing installation methods, and strengthening infrastructure (e.g., submarine cable protection and maintenance). There is also an emphasis on comprehensive planning, including site selection, environmental considerations, and operational strategies to ensure sustainable growth in this sector.  \n\n(Source: Contextual information provided in the database.)', 'contexts': '. Solutions include strengthening the protection measures for submarine cables, regular check-up and maintenance, and the use of new materials etc."}\n{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "May I ask, what are the advantages of marine energy technology?\\n", "output": "Compared to other forms of energy, marine energy technology has the following advantages: it\'s renewable, stable, low carbon, environmentally frie