fret is prevalent in Shanghai, Zhejiang, and Fujian, while carp, silver carp, eel, bass, and mullet are widely distributed across the region. Sharks are also noted as significant marine ecological resources in the area. This information is derived from the provided context.', 'contexts': ': "The issue should be negotiated and resolved within the framework of international law, such as developing joint development plans, among others."}\n{"task_type": "Extraction", "input": "Extract the most common fish resources from the east china sea.", "output": "The most common fish resources in the East China Sea include croaker, pomfret, carp, silver carp, eel, bass, mullet, shark, and so on. Among them, croaker is one of the most important fishery resources in the East China Sea and is mainly distributed in the waters of Zhejiang, Fujian, Jiangsu and other places. Pomfret is mainly distributed in the waters of Shanghai, Zhejiang, Fujian and other places. Carp, silver carp, eel, bass, mullet, etc., are widely distributed and common fish resources in the East China Sea. Sharks are one of the important marine ecological resources in the East China Sea."}{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Write a report on marine litter management, within 200 words.", "output": "Marine waste management refers to a series of actions involving the cleaning, transport, processing, and disposal of waste in the ocean. Currently, our country has established a comprehensive marine waste management system and has been cooperating with the international community to protect the marine environment and ecology."}\n', 'reference': 'Common fish resources in the East China Sea include yellow croaker, pomfret, carp, silver carp, bass, horse mackerel, eel, pomfret, and shark.'}{'question': 'Share your views on typhoon forecasts.', 'answer': '\n\nBased on the provided context, typhoon forecasts rely on real-time meteorological data and monitoring of atmospheric and oceanic conditions. For instance, the forecast mentions that a low-pressure system in the South China Sea is expected to bring strong winds (force 7-9, with gusts up to force 10) to the southeast of Hainan Island, while a weak typhoon in the East China Sea may approach northern Fujian. Such predictions highlight the dynamic nature of typhoon behavior, influenced by factors like pressure systems, wind patterns, and geographic locations. Continuous monitoring and updates are critical, as typhoon trajectories and intensities can shift rapidly, requiring timely adjustments to warnings and preparedness measures. The collaboration between scientific institutions (e.g., Chinese Academy of Sciences, Ocean University of China) also underscores the importance of advanced observation tools, such as marine survey ships, in improving forecast accuracy. However, typhoon predictions remain probabilistic, emphasizing the need for public vigilance and adaptive responses.', 'contexts': 'f the Chinese Academy of Sciences, and the marine scientific survey ships \\"East Sea No.1\\" and \\"East Sea No.2\\" of the Ocean University of China."}\n{"task_type": "Editing", "input": "Write a forecast article about typhoon information based on the latest meteorological observation data.", "output": "Affected by the low pressure in the South China Sea, it is predicted that from the night of the 23rd to the daytime of the 24th, the southeast sea area of Hainan Island will experience south or southwest winds of force 7-9, with some areas reaching force 10 and above, and the central pressure will decrease, with 1-2 force gusts; At the same time, a weak typhoon in the East China Sea is likely to enter the area east of the coast of northern Fujian tomorrow afternoon and will continue to move towards the north eastward. We will continue to monitor and release the latest forecast information."}{"task_type": "Question-Answering", "input": "Why does deep-sea mining contain numerous treasures to be excavated?", "output": "Deep-sea minerals are formed by